for (initialization; condition; update) {
    // code to be executed repeatedly
}

The initialization step is run once at the beginning of the loop.  The condition is checked at the beginning of each loop iteration.  If it is true, the code inside the loop is executed.  After the code is executed, the update step is executed.  This step is run once at the end of each loop iteration.  

Here’s an example of a for loop that prints the values from 0 to 4:

int i;
for (i = 0; i <= 4; i++) {
    printf("%d ", i);
}

